==Strategy==
Once one of the most notorious and difficult stages in the entire game, Floor 47 can still pose a challenge to the unprepared. While there are a couple of ways to clear this stage, like using anti-Traitless units to endure the stage or getting a huge [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] chain early, the easiest and most consistent way to clear this level is to use a bunch of Research combos alongside rushers and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]. Stone is insanely powerful on this stage, being able to bait Corrupted Moneko's hits, walling against Brollows or forcing out an attack from Owlbrow. With five slots of Research combos, Stone is essentially able to singlehandedly wall the whole stage. From there, rushers like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] can chip down each threat. The most vital part of this stage is making sure you use Stone to bait out a Puffsley hit instead of Moneko, given that if Puffsley moves forward you have just lost a ton of room to work with. Corrupted Moneko's huge Wave hurts, but losing your ground to Puffsley is worse.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can can provide great burst damage to handle any of the enemies present in this stage, but needs proper timing in order to hit Corrupted Moneko and maybe Puffsley.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] or [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: Can help deal with Tackeys, and the latter can help chip.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]]: Excellent units to help control Corrupted Moneko.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Its wave attacks can deal significant quantities of chip damage versus the peons, specifically the Brollows and Tackeys, while also forcing Puffsley to stagger at a distance.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Brollows come in waves of 2, Bullet train can quickly kill one, relieving lots of pressure and getting Extra Money in the process.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Especially after Talents, Bahamut's Explosion is able to rack up insane amounts of damage and easily clear out stacks of Owlbrows or Tackeys sitting in the back. It is even possible to have him one-chain Puffsley and greatly reduce the difficulty of the stage, as demonstrated in the Walkthrough section.

===Recommended Ubers===
*Nukers such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]], [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]], and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] will work well on Puffsley. [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] could work, but a specific setup is required.

